# Call-site ledger of markdown2 at 150454e3ba02caa3994d19cb5a8344fc92f3ce13.
# Hand-written from the source (lib/markdown2.py); judgements in markdown2.md.
#
# The scope rules A, B1-B5 and C are in macro-benchmark/README.md;
# markdown2.md ("Scope rules") shows how this ledger applies them. In short:
# - The methods that @mark_stage decorates (16, markdown2.py:579-2108) are
#   bound to the closure mark_stage.wrapper.inner; a call self._do_x(...)
#   runs inner, and inner runs the original through func (255:24).
# - The module registers 20 extra classes at import (4325-4344). Public
#   Extra.register also admits LinkProcessor and GFMItalicAndBoldProcessor
#   to inner's stage lists; both are also instantiated directly (1556, 2055).
#   ItalicAndBoldProcessor remains abstract.
# - Receivers named by the code: self.md is the Markdown; patterns (class
#   attributes and locals from re.compile) are re.Pattern, their results
#   re.Match; text values are str; self.extras, self.urls, self.html_blocks
#   and the other tables are dicts; the option values of extras are client
#   objects, except where a TypedDict or an isinstance test fixes dict (B4).
default reject markdown2._memoized.__repr__: no _memoized object is formatted or converted to a string at this site; the only _memoized objects are the module globals _xml_oneliner_re_from_tab_width and _hr_tag_re_from_tab_width (markdown2.py:4589, 4609), which the package only calls; the operands of %, str.format, f-strings, str() and print() are strs, ints, bools, floats, tuples of those, re.Match groups, Stage members or client values
default reject markdown2.Admonitions.sub, markdown2.Alerts.sub, markdown2.FencedCodeBlocks.sub, markdown2.ItalicAndBoldProcessor.sub, markdown2.MiddleWordEm.sub, markdown2.PyShell.sub, markdown2.Tables.sub, markdown2.Wavedrom.sub, markdown2.WikiTables.sub: the call is re.sub or the sub method of a compiled re.Pattern (a class attribute, or a local that re.compile made), not the sub method of an extra; where an extra passes its own self.sub as the replacement callback, the site accepts that one method explicitly

